From 8898d02bbc2f154bbf0a1fe1ff8f76a16011aa22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:33:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] save-sync: add --dry-run

Print what a sync would do as one JSON object on stdout and change
nothing: no upload, download or delete, and no creation of a missing
local directory. The action is the classification sync() acts on,
including its empty-side rules; --skip-* and --force-* are not applied,
so a launcher can show a conflict to the user before choosing one.
The report names each side's file count and newest update time, and
the files in each category.
---
 gogdl/args.py  |  6 ++++++
 gogdl/saves.py | 56 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 59 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gogdl/args.py b/gogdl/args.py
